---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { site, url } from '../lib/url'
---

<Base title="About" current="about" description="About Mufaddal Hirani: final-year B.Sc. IT student in Mumbai, builder of Lyrigen, with hands-on experience installing CCTV and access-control systems since 2020.">
  <section class="wrap intro">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="h1">From cables<br />to <em>code.</em></h1>
    </div>
    <img
      class="portrait"
      src={url('media/portrait-800.webp')}
      srcset={`${url('media/portrait-400.webp')} 400w, ${url('media/portrait-800.webp')} 800w`}
      sizes="(min-width: 900px) 320px, 60vw"
      width="800"
      height="1067"
      alt="Portrait of Mufaddal Hirani in a light grey shirt against a plain background."
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="lede">
        I’m Mufaddal, a final-year B.Sc. Information Technology student in the Mumbai area. I like taking an idea
        all the way to something people can download and use, and I care about the details that make software feel finished.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2">Hardware first</h2>
      <p>
        I started with my hands. Since 2020 I’ve helped in my family’s security-systems business, installing
        <strong>IP, Wi-Fi and analog CCTV cameras</strong> and <strong>biometric attendance and access systems</strong>
        at a school, a construction site, shops and residential and commercial buildings. That meant running
        low-voltage cabling, mounting and aiming cameras, setting up recorders and viewing software, and explaining
        the finished system to the people who would use it. It taught me that technology only counts when it works on site,
        for the person in front of you.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2">Then support, then software</h2>
      <p>
        In 2025 I joined <strong>Concentrix</strong> as a <strong>Level 2 Digital Case Manager</strong> for Optus, an
        Australian telecom company. After two months of training I handled home Wi-Fi cases that first-level support
        couldn’t solve: calling customers back, troubleshooting step by step and following up until the problem was
        fixed. I resolved 50–60 escalated cases in my first month on the floor. I left in September 2025 to focus on my degree.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m completing my B.Sc. IT at Rizvi College (University of Mumbai). I repeated my second year in 2025–26 and
        cleared every outstanding exam in 2026. That moved me onto the revised NEP&nbsp;2020 curriculum, which adds AI
        modules and a <strong>minor in Statistics</strong>. I expect to graduate in mid-2027.
      </p>
      <p>
        Alongside my studies I build software I want to use myself: <a href={url('work/lyrigen/')}>Lyrigen</a>, a music
        player with AI-timed lyrics, and <a href={url('work/extensions/')}>browser extensions</a> for YouTube.
        Music is the thread through all of it: I play electric and acoustic guitar and produce music, which is why my
        biggest project is an audio app.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2">How I work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Finish things.</strong> A released, documented version beats a perfect plan.</li>
        <li><strong>Write it down.</strong> READMEs, code comments that explain <em>why</em>, and honest changelogs.</li>
        <li><strong>Respect the user.</strong> Local-first where possible, no tracking, and accessible interfaces.</li>
        <li><strong>Use good tools well.</strong> I use AI coding assistants to move faster. The design decisions, the testing and the responsibility for every change are mine.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="h2">Germany</h2>
      <p>
        After graduating I want to work in Germany. I like how German engineering teams value thoroughness,
        documentation and doing things properly. I’m learning German, and I’m open to internships and junior roles,
        remote or on site.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <dl class="facts">
        <div><dt>Based in</dt><dd>{site.location}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Languages</dt><dd>English (fluent) · Hindi, Urdu, Gujarati, Marathi · Arabic (reading) · German (learning)</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Education</dt><dd>B.Sc. IT, University of Mumbai, minor in Statistics, 2027</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Outside work</dt><dd>Guitar, music production, treks</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href={url('cv/')}>View CV</a>
        <a class="button" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Email me</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro { display: grid; gap: 40px; padding-top: clamp(48px, 8vw, 96px); align-items: end; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .intro { grid-template-columns: 1fr 320px; } }
  .portrait { width: min(320px, 70vw); border-radius: var(--radius); border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--sunken); }
  .prose .lede { max-width: none; margin-bottom: 1.4em; color: var(--text); }
  .actions { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 40px; }
</style>
